=== P3 Feature view 0008 ResultPanel (Android) ===

--- Surface notes (honesty: documented adaptations) ---
Web source: web/src/features/admin/components/devtools/ResultPanel.tsx (pure presentational).
Module Gradle path is :android (settings.gradle.kts: 'every P3/A* prompt gate addresses :android:');
the prompt's ':app:' is the template token for that module. Tasks below use :android: to match.
States reproduced = the web source's complete set: error / result(+copy) / idle.
loading/stale/offline are N/A: the source binds NO data hooks (no fetch, no freshness) -> nothing to
load, go stale, or lose connectivity. No state was narrowed; these branches do not exist in the source.
idleMessage is a required, caller-supplied localized String: the web default literal 'No result yet' is
not reproducible as a Kotlin literal (no-English-literals rule) and has no generated i18n key (the web
uses a literal, not a t() call), so the localized text is the caller's responsibility (as web 'title' is).
Container tint -> GlassPanel border accent (the sanctioned native mapping of the web glow/tint affordance).
Tests are pure-JVM (the unit-test classpath has no Robolectric/Compose-UI-test); the per-state projection
test IS the snapshot of the render-ready output, and bodyText is the body's accessible (TalkBack) text.
A Compose UI test (androidTest/.../resultpanel/ResultPanelUiTest.kt) covers on-device render + a11y; it is
ktlint-clean and compiles (member-call .assertDoesNotExist(); absent from the compiler error list). The
gate does NOT compile androidTest; that source set is pre-existingly broken by 8 UNRELATED widget UI tests
that wrongly 'import androidx.compose.ui.test.assertDoesNotExist' (a member, not a top-level symbol) — out
of this artifact's allowed files, so left untouched. connectedAndroidTest is a device job, not in this gate.

